<title>PHILIPPINES: ATI to handle Hanjin port needs in Manila.</title>
<headline>ATI to handle Hanjin port needs in Manila.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Port operator Asian Terminals Inc said on Wednesday it had signed a three-year contract to provide container handling and related port services to Hanjin Shipping Co Ltd vessels visiting Manila.</p>
<p>The contract was signed at the launching of Hanjin's Philippine-Japan Express route which covers the ports of Tokyo, Yokohama and Osaka in Japan, the Pusan port in South Korea, the Manila South Harbour and the Jakarta port in Indonesia.</p>
